@startuml SALUD_Module_70_observability
title Module 70 — System Observability: Errors, Latency, SQL, Instances, Dependencies and Alerts
(schema: observability)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide circle

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Source: docs/trabajo/2026-10-31-portal-observabilidad-gobierno/02-observabilidad-sistema.md
' §4 (modelo de datos) and PLAN.md §4 F1 (item 1). Franja F1, hito H1.S1 of that plan.
'
' WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS. The API measures HTTP traffic into a single jsonb row per
' minute (time_series.service_sli_series), groups no errors, keeps no per-SQL
' statistics and has no registry of running processes. This module gives the
' "System" panel of the observability portal relational, indexed, idempotent tables
' instead. Every table here is PLATFORM data: there is no tenant dimension.
'
' DECISION D-F1-1 — no column is named `tenant_id`.
'   2026-08-05_tenant_rls.sql enables ROW LEVEL SECURITY (policy tenant_isolation:
'   tenant_id = app.current_tenant_id OR app.system_context) on EVERY table that has a
'   `tenant_id uuid` column, nullable or not. A platform row has no tenant, so with
'   that column name every INSERT by the application role would fail WITH CHECK and
'   every SELECT would return nothing outside a SYSTEM context. The only tenant these
'   tables ever carry is the tenant of the ACTOR that caused an error, so it is named
'   `actor_tenant_id` (plain uuid, no FK: telemetry must survive the deletion of the
'   tenant and must never block it) and the RLS patch does not reach it. The two tables that DO carry an actor
'   tenant (error_events here, telemetry.client_error_events) get an explicit policy set in
'   SQL/patches/2026-10-31_v4280_*.sql §6b (same GUC pattern: app.current_tenant_id /
'   app.system_context): SELECT own tenant or system context, INSERT unconditional (public
'   ingestion does not know the tenant), DELETE system context only. NULL actor tenant =>
'   visible to system context only. Policies are not expressible in the .puml generators.
'
' DECISION D-F1-2 — the time series are RELATIONAL here, not TIMESERIES_MEASUREMENT
'   entities in module 58.
'   (a) module 58 is emitted by gen_nosql.py as NoSQL/58_time_series_timescaledb/*.sql,
'       whose first statement is CREATE EXTENSION timescaledb; it is not part of
'       apply_all.sql, and a plain PostgreSQL (the local and CI environments) cannot
'       apply it. The relational DDL below applies clean without the extension.
'   (b) the API converts tables to hypertables at boot (physical.catalog.ts,
'       TIMESERIES_TABLES, migrate_data => TRUE) when TimescaleDB is present. These
'       tables are written to be convertible as they are: the partitioning column is
'       part of every PRIMARY KEY, there is no UNIQUE index without it, and no table
'       is the target of a foreign key. See the HYPERTABLE POLICY note for the
'       per-table chunk and retention that the API must register (the retention of
'       module 58 style: drop_chunks by age; DELETE stays allowed on every <<LOG>>
'       table, only UPDATE is forbidden — module 33).
'   (c) the PRIMARY KEY of a minute series IS its idempotency key (the plan's
'       uq_*_minute_key): the retry of a flush does INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
'       A second UNIQUE index on the same columns would double the write cost of the
'       hottest table of the module for nothing, so it is not declared.
'
' DECISION D-F1-3 — the high-rate series carry instance_id WITHOUT a foreign key.
'   A flush must never fail because the instance heartbeat row is late or was purged;
'   losing a minute of metrics is worse than an orphan uuid. error_events, which is
'   low-rate and joined constantly, DOES reference instances.
'
' DECISION D-F1-4 — alert severity reuses platform_ops incident severities
'   (CONCEPTS.INCIDENT_SEV_* in the API; the column is a plain *_concept_id). No new
'   severity vocabulary. Alerts open/update platform_ops.health_incidents.
'
' DECISION D-F1-5 — `client_error_events` of 02 §4.1 (D-03) is NOT created here. The
'   browser/mobile error table is telemetry.client_error_events (module 28, per
'   03-uso-errores-heatmap.md §4.3), with the longer 90-day retention. One table, one owner.
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_70_observability
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  Answers "is the system healthy, what is failing, how often, since when and where
  does the time go" for platform operators: grouped errors with a fingerprint and a
  request id to jump to the trace, HTTP latency histograms per route and status,
  SQL statistics per normalized statement, a registry of API and worker processes
  with heartbeats, dependency probes, slow-request samples, and threshold alerts that
  open platform_ops incidents. No PHI: messages are redacted, SQL has no literals,
  actors appear only as a keyed hash (OBSERVABILITY_ACTOR_HASH_SECRET, D-02).
end note

