note as HYPERTABLE_POLICY_diagram_70_observability
  HYPERTABLE POLICY (declared for physical.catalog.ts / TS_RETENTION_POLICIES; the DDL
  of this module is plain relational and does not require TimescaleDB)
  table                         time column   chunk   retention (drop_chunks)
  error_events                  occurred_at   1 day   90 days
  http_request_minute_series    time          1 day   14 days   (hourly aggregate 400 d, daily 5 y)
  sql_statement_minute_series   time          1 day   14 days
  worker_tick_minute_series     time          1 day   30 days
  slow_request_samples          time          1 day   30 days
  dependency_probe_runs         time          1 day   30 days
  alert_evaluations             (ordinary table, not a hypertable)  retention 400 days by job
  Convertibility contract: every PRIMARY KEY above contains the time column; no UNIQUE
  index without it; no foreign key points AT these tables (error_events and
  dependency_probe_runs point out to ordinary tables, which Timescale allows).
  Planned continuous aggregates (API, F2): observability_http_hourly/_daily,
  observability_sql_hourly, observability_errors_hourly. Until the worker that refreshes
  them is deployed (D-04), observability.rollup_watermarks drives manual idempotent rollups.
end note

note as CAPTURE_RULES_diagram_70_observability
  CAPTURE RULES (contract with the API)
  - error_groups.fingerprint = sha256(source|code|reason|exception_type|method|route_template|
    top-3 own frames). occurrences_total only grows by rows REALLY inserted in error_events.
  - route_template is always a template, never a URL; sample_message / message_redacted are
    redacted (500 chars); frames hold relative paths and no code columns; violations_json
    holds {field, constraint} only.
  - error_events.actor_hash = HMAC(user_id, secret); the user id is never stored (D-02).
  - http_status 0 = aborted request. flush_seq is the ordinal of the flush inside the minute
    for that instance, so a retried flush hits ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
  - operation_key is part of the SQL minute key, so it is NOT NULL: the API writes UNKNOWN when
    the statement ran outside a controller operation. At most 5000 query_hash per minute per
    instance; the excess is aggregated under query_hash '__overflow__'.
  - Histograms are CUMULATIVE ("le" columns); the http `requests` column is the +Inf bucket.
  - sampled_because: slow | error | random. Dependency status: up | degraded | down | not_probed.
  - instances.status: starting | running | draining | stopped. instances.kind: API | WORKER.
  - error_groups.state_concept_id: observability:ERROR_GROUP_STATE_{NEW,SEEN,RESOLVED,IGNORED}.
  - error_groups.source and error_events.source: api | worker | web.
end note

